# ── How exclusion works now (this changed in Stage 2) ──────────────────
#
# In Stage 1 this file WAS the privacy mechanism: the site was served
# straight from the repo, so keeping a file out of the upload kept it off
# the web.
#
# There is a build step now. Vercel serves only dist/, and dist/ contains
# exactly two things: the JavaScript bundle, and a verbatim copy of
# public/. So the two rules that actually keep something off the site are:
#
#   1. It is not in public/.  Everything in public/ ships, no exceptions.
#   2. No routed component imports it.  An un-imported module is not in
#      the bundle.
#
# This file is now only an upload-size and tidiness measure. Do not rely
# on it to keep anything private — check dist/ instead.

# ── Porting reference: the original static site ────────────────────────
# The nine hand-authored pages and their .jsx, kept readable while each
# one is ported. Deleted when Stage 2 is complete. Nothing imports them,
# so they are not in the bundle either way.
#
# Includes project-admin-shell.html and legacy/frames/ — the non-public
# UiPath Admin Shell case study. It has no route (brief 2.3) and is
# imported by nothing, which is what keeps it off the site.
legacy/

# ── Image and video masters, kept for re-export ────────────────────────
# The 600px PNG originals for the About marquee, and the ProRes video
# sources. The site serves the WebP and MP4 built from these.
masters/

# ── Internal documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# HANDOFF, MIGRATION_BRIEF, PROJECT_CONTEXT, DESIGN_SYSTEM, CLAUDE.
*.md
